regular acquire barriers disallow any instruction from escaping the load following the barrier.

likewise release barriers disallow any stores/loads from escaping below the barrier

check out these depenent variants ... very interesting.
http://wiki.dinkumware.com/twiki/pub/Wg21oxford/EvolutionWorkingGroup/ParallelCExperience.2007.04.17b.pdf

=========
load dependent acquire: essentially only prevent those instructions from reordering that have a data 
dependency on the load following the barrier.


store dependent release:
likewise disallow any dependent load/stores from escaping below the barrier but unrelated ones can escape

